course: dictionary
lesson: 2613
title: Derision: laughing at someone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Derision means unkind laughter or comments that show someone thinks a person or idea is stupid or worthless. It is mocking. «The inventor's idea was met with derision» means people laughed at it and called it silly.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like «hoots» and «with» show that people are laughing, not listening. «The crowd greeted her plan with hoots of derision» tells you the crowd was mocking her plan. A person being laughed at is «an object of derision».
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mock Turtle's school subjects are a joke made of twisted words. Derision sounds like division, so it is one of the silly subject names. Always check the dictionary when you are not sure.
fact: Derision means unkind laughter or mocking comments.
fact: «An object of derision» means someone who is being laughed at.
fact: «Hoots of derision» means loud, mocking laughter.
fact: Derision is a form of bullying, because laughing at someone hurts their feelings.
fact: Inventors and explorers have sometimes been met with derision before their ideas were proven right.
exercise: «The inventor's idea was met with derision at first.» What does derision mean here? | Warm applause and cheering | Long, careful study | A sudden storm | *Unkind laughing and mocking
exercise: «Hoots of derision filled the hall when he stumbled on stage.» What were the hoots? | Sleepy yawns | *Loud, unkind laughter | Happy singing
exercise: Which phrase means someone is being laughed at? | *an object of derision | a gift of time | a piece of cake | a sign of respect
test: Mia says «derision» is mid, just say «laughing». Why is derision the better word? | *It shows the laughing is unkind and mocking | It means happy laughing at a party | It means the same as cheering | It is shorter
test: Which example shows derision? | Kids cheering for Sam's drawing | Kids helping Sam pick up his books | Kids quietly reading in the library | *Kids laughing at Sam's wobbly drawing and calling it silly
exam: In «Ambition, Distraction, Uglification and Derision», what is the joke? | They are the names of four Alice characters | They are real school subjects with their correct names | They are the Gryphon's favourite sweets | *They are twisted school words that sound like the real subjects, such as Derision for division
